  const newBoardEls = [...document.querySelectorAll(FLIP_SEL)].filter(el => !knownBoardUids.has(el.getAttribute('data-uid')));
  newBoardEls.forEach(el=> knownBoardUids.add(el.getAttribute('data-uid')));
  // Bugfix (2026-09-17, root cause of the RESIDUAL teleport a live diagnostic still caught
  // after the fitBattlefieldZoom rewrite — a card snapping up to 657px in one frame with
  // `battlefield transform` confirmed `none` throughout, so it wasn't the zoom fix's own bug
  // recurring). A brand-new card is deliberately excluded from Flip's targets (see the
  // flipTargets comment below) and stays in NORMAL DOCUMENT FLOW the whole time, governed
  // purely by its own opacity/scale/y/rotate entrance tween. But Flip's OTHER targets — every
  // already-existing card on this same side — go `position:absolute` for the whole `dur` of
  // their own tween (that's what `absolute:true` does below), which pulls them OUT of this
  // row's flex layout for that entire window. With them gone from the flow, `justify-content:
  // center` has only the still-in-flow new card(s) (plus invisible empty-slot spacers) left to
  // lay out — so the new card visibly settles, mid-tween, at a DIFFERENT position than its true
  // final one. The instant Flip's tween finishes and reverts its targets back to static flow,
  // the layout recomputes with everyone present again, and the new card — which has no tween
  // of its own still running by then — SNAPS instantly to its real position with zero easing.
