  // tween is created, not lazily once the animation frame ticks — so measuring after that call
  // would capture the ALREADY-CORRUPTED mid-transition layout instead of the true, still-
  // everyone-in-flow final one, which is worse than not pinning at all. Pinning costs nothing
  // visually (the new card is already exactly there) but stops the live flex algorithm from
  // moving it out from under its own entrance tween while existing siblings come and go from
  // the flow around it. Both groups are put back into normal flow together once both this row's
  // entrance tween AND Flip's own tween have finished (see the settle delayedCall further
