      // called) for exactly why the write has to be deferred: Flip.from() itself needs to see
      // this new card still sitting in normal flex flow (taking up its real slot) when it reads
      // its OWN targets' true resting position, or every existing card's Flip animation ends at
      // the wrong spot — a residual jump that survived the entrance-vs-Flip pinning (Cause A) and
      // the release-timing (Cause D) fixes. The measurement itself is still taken now, before
      // anything moves, so it reflects this card's correct final resting box.
      newElRects = newBoardEls.map(el=>({el, left:el.offsetLeft, top:el.offsetTop, width:el.offsetWidth, height:el.offsetHeight}));
      if(window.__DEBUG_RENDER__) newElRects.forEach(r=>console.log('[measure]', r.el.getAttribute('data-uid'), 'left=',r.left,'top=',r.top));
