      // right"): a sweep continuation hit (ev.sweep, reaching a second/third target further
      // down the flank) gets a side-to-side wag instead of the plain single-target lunge below,
      // so a sweep visibly reads as "swinging across the row" rather than one clean jab. The
      // wag direction follows leanX (toward whichever target this particular sweep hit landed
      // on), same signal the single-target lean below uses, just amplified into a real swing.
      const wagDir = opts.leanX>=0 ? 1 : -1;
